{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1432737-suggestions-for-a-dark-ages-prince-of-constanta","id":1432737,"title":"Suggestions for a Dark Ages Prince of Constanta?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-19T18:02:05-08:00","id":1432737,"title":"Suggestions for a Dark Ages Prince of Constanta?","content":"I'm looking for ideas anyone might have for the prince of Constan\u021ba, Romania, in a Dark Ages game during the year 1198, specially one that isn't Tzimisce. Nothing too in depth needed. The coterie stopped in Constanta on their way to Bistritz (I'm running a heavily modified version of Transylvania Chronicles), and while there caused a commotion that would at the very least have them questioned by the prince. I've checked to see if there was a canon prince I could use or modify, but I haven't had any luck finding one for Constanta.<br /> <br /> Here's the Wikipedia entry on the city of Constanta, in case anyone would like it. It's the oldest continuously inhabited city in Romania, founded around 600 BC, and is on the coast of the Black Sea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constan%C8%9Ba\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/CasinoCT2026.jpg/1280px-CasinoCT2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constan%C8%9Ba\" target=\"_blank\"> Constan\u021ba - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constan%C8%9Ba\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constan%C8%9Ba </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}